te person, i.e. (by implication) an ignoramus (compare \"idiot\")","p":null,"t":"idiotes","g":"uninstructed","fb":[],"v":[27034,28689,28696,28697,28990]},"G2333":{"l":"Θευδᾶς","x":"Theudâs","d":"Theudas, an Israelite","p":null,"t":"theudas","g":"Theudas","fb":[["theudas","Theudas","Man living at the time of the New Testament","Gamaliel's example of a movement that died with its leader. Theudas raised a following, he was killed, and it came to nothing. Josephus mentions a rebel Theudas around AD 44, later than Gamaliel's speech, and whether that is the same man has never been settled.","person",1]],"v":[27094]},"G2314":{"l":"θεομάχος","x":"theomáchos","d":"an opponent of deity","p":null,"t":"theomachos","g":"fighting against God","fb":[],"v":[27097]},"G2371":{"l":"θυμομαχέω","x":"thymomachéō","d":"to be in a furious fight, i.e. (figuratively) to be exasperated","p":null,"t":"thymomacheo","g":"furiously angry","fb":[],"v":[27356]},"G2363":{"l":"Θυάτειρα","x":"Thyáteira","d":"Thyatira, a place in Asia Minor","p":null,"t":"thyateira","g":"Thyatira","fb":[["thyatira","Thyatira","","A trading city in the Roman province of Asia, known for its guilds, especially the dyers. Lydia, the seller of purple cloth Paul met at Philippi, came from there, and Revelation sends one of its seven letters to the church there.","place",4]],"v":[27496,30703,30730,30736]},"G2332":{"l":"Θεσσαλονίκη","x":"Thessaloníkē","d":"Thessalonice, a place in Asia Minor","p":null,"t":"thessalonike","g":"Thessalonica","fb":[["thessalonica","Thessalonica","","The capital of Macedonia, a busy port on the Via Egnatia. Paul preached in the synagogue there for a few weeks before opposition drove him on to Berea. Luke calls the city officials politarchs, an unusual title.","place",5]],"v":[27523,27533,27535,29452,29874]},"G2394":{"l":"Ἰάσων","x":"Iásōn","d":"about to cure; Jason, a Christian","p":null,"t":"iason","g":"Jason","fb":[["jason","Jason","Man living at the time of the New Testament","Paul and Silas stayed with him in Thessalonica. When a mob came for Paul and could not find him, they dragged Jason before the city officials instead, charging him with harbouring men who defied Caesar's decrees, and he had to post bond to go free.","person",5]],"v":[27527,27528,27529,27531,28355]},"G2304":{"l":"θεῖος","x":"theîos","d":"godlike (neuter as noun, divinity)","p":null,"t":"theios","g":"divine","fb":[],"v":[27551,30476,30477]},"G2302":{"l":"θέατρον","x":"théatron","d":"a place for public show (\"theatre\"), i.e. general audience-room; by implication, a show itself (figuratively)","p":null,"t":"theatron","g":"theatre","fb":[],"v":[27613,27615,28437]},"G2331":{"l":"Θεσσαλονικεύς","x":"Thessalonikeús","d":"a Thessalonican, i.e. inhabitant of Thessalonice","p":null,"t":"thessalonikeus","g":"of the Thessalonians","fb":[["thessalonian","Thessalonian","Thessalonica","Someone from Thessalonica, the port in Roman Macedonia where Paul planted a church and then had to leave in a hurry. His two letters to them are among the earliest writing in the New Testament.","place",3]],"v":[27628,27855,29555,29644]},"G2376":{"l":"θυρίς","x":"thyrís","d":"an aperture, i.e. window","p":null,"t":"thyris","g":"a window","fb":[],"v":[27633,29017]},"G2356":{"l":"θρησκεία","x":"thrēskeía","d":"ceremonial observance","p":null,"t":"threskeia","g":"religion","fb":[],"v":[27826,29506,30286,30287]},"G2329":{"l":"θέρμη","x":"thérmē","d":"warmth","p":null,"t":"therme","g":"heat","fb":[],"v":[27900]},"G2305":{"l":"θειότης","x":"theiótēs","d":"divinity (abstractly)","p":null,"t":"theiotes","g":"divinity","fb":[],"v":[27948]},"G2319":{"l":"θεοστυγής","x":"theostygḗs","d":"hateful to God, i.e. impious","p":null,"t":"theostyges","g":"hateful to God","fb":[],"v":[27958]},"G2349":{"l":"θνητός","x":"thnētós","d":"liable to die","p":null,"t":"thnetos","g":"mortal","fb":[],"v":[28078,28125,28766,28767,28865,28876]},"G2339":{"l":"θήρα","x":"thḗra","d":"hunting, i.e. (figuratively) destruction","p":null,"t":"thera","g":