res, an Egyptian","p":null,"t":"iambres","g":"Jambres","fb":[["jambres","Jambres","Man living at the time of the New Testament","Paul names Jannes and Jambres as the men who opposed Moses, and so a warning about anyone who resists the truth. Exodus has Pharaoh's magicians copy some of the signs but never names them; the names come from Jewish tradition.","person",1]],"v":[29855]},"G2315":{"l":"θεόπνευστος","x":"theópneustos","d":"divinely breathed in","p":null,"t":"theopneustos","g":"God-breathed","fb":[],"v":[29863]},"G2308":{"l":"θέλησις","x":"thélēsis","d":"determination (properly, the act), i.e. option","p":null,"t":"thelesis","g":"will","fb":[],"v":[29975]},"G2324":{"l":"θεράπων","x":"therápōn","d":"a menial attendant (as if cherishing)","p":null,"t":"therapon","g":"a servant","fb":[],"v":[29994]},"G2369":{"l":"θυμιαστήριον","x":"thymiastḗrion","d":"a place of fumigation, i.e. the alter of incense (in the Temple)","p":null,"t":"thymiasterion","g":"altar of incense","fb":[],"v":[30103]},"G2301":{"l":"θεατρίζω","x":"theatrízō","d":"to expose as a spectacle","p":null,"t":"theatrizo","g":"being made a spectacle","fb":[],"v":[30160]},"G2366":{"l":"θύελλα","x":"thýella","d":"","p":null,"t":"thyella","g":"to storm","fb":[],"v":[30224]},"G2357":{"l":"θρησκός","x":"thrēskós","d":"ceremonious in worship (as demonstrative), i.e. pious","p":null,"t":"threskos","g":"religious","fb":[],"v":[30286]},"G2393":{"l":"ἴασπις","x":"íaspis","d":"\"jasper\", a gem","p":null,"t":"iaspis","g":"jasper","fb":[],"v":[30766,31059,31066,31067]},"G2306":{"l":"θειώδης","x":"theiṓdēs","d":"sulphur-like, i.e. sulphurous","p":null,"t":"theiodes","g":"brimstone","fb":[],"v":[30852]},"G2367":{"l":"θύϊνος","x":"thýïnos","d":"denoting a certain fragrant tree); made of citron-wood","p":null,"t":"thyinos","g":"citron","fb":[],"v":[31000]}}